             Loki
______________________________

Grafana Loki is a open-source log aggregation system used to collect ,store and query logs from applications and infrastructures

In simple Words: 

Imagine your e-commerce application has multiple microservices:
* Product catalogt
* Product Inventory
* Order Management
* Shipping and Handling
* Profile Management
* Contact Support

Each service generate logs when it runs

For example: 

Product catalog Logs: 
INFO: Product service started
INFO: Connected to MongoDB
INFO: GET /api/products - 200 OK
ERROR: Failed to retrieve product

Order Management Logs: 
INFO: Order service started
INFO: New order received
INFO: Order saved successfully
ERROR: MongoDB connection timeout

The problem is that every application generate the logs separately 
If you want to troubleshoot and error , you would otherwise need to access 
individual kubernetes Pods and inspect their logs
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
This becomes difficult  when you have many microservices and multiple replicas



Loki solves this problem by collecting logs from different sources and making them searchable from one centralized location.

